# Kirara Server Studio Software License Agreement

> Version v2.0 | Effective: November 15, 2026

**IMPORTANT:** This Agreement is a legal agreement between you and the Kirara Server Development Team (the "Developer") concerning your use of the Kirara Server Studio software (the "Software"). Please read it in full before installing or using the Software. Article 4 (User Data and Privacy), Article 6 (System Permissions and Security), Article 8 (Disclaimer) and Article 9 (Limitation of Liability) directly affect your rights. By clicking "Agree", installing, or otherwise using the Software, you confirm that you have read and accepted this Agreement. If you do not agree, do not install or use the Software.

## Article 1 Definitions

1.1 **The Software** means the Kirara Server Studio client and all of its components, modules, built-in Schemes, interfaces, icons and documentation, together with any updates, patches and upgrade packages provided by the Developer, including the built-in App Store, Download Manager, Notification Center and community features.

1.2 **Services and Server.** Services means the remote services you access after creating an Instance and binding a Scheme, including media, live streaming, cloud storage, mail, team collaboration, virtualization, remote desktop, OpenVPN and others, as actually made available in the Software. Server means the Kirara Server platform operated by the Developer, which provides account authentication, template and Scheme configuration distribution, comment storage, notification push, feeds, asset caching and cloud sync.

1.3 **User and Developer.** User means the natural person or legal entity that installs and uses the Software, i.e. the contracting party to this Agreement. Developer means the Kirara Server Development Team and its authorized entities.

1.4 **Instance, Scheme and Token.** An Instance is a configuration unit you create in the Software, either a "User Instance" or a "Service Instance". A Scheme is the feature template bound to an Instance. A Token is the set of account credentials used to sign in to, or call, the corresponding service.

1.5 **App Store and Plugins.** The App Store is the built-in entry point for browsing, downloading and managing plugins and resources. Plugins are third-party components and extensions obtained through the App Store or other channels and installed on the device or in the Software's directory.

1.6 **Cloud Sync** means the feature that encrypts and uploads an "Instance package" or "Token package" to the Server, and can download and restore it.

1.7 **Community Content** means content you submit through the Software that may be visible to other users, including comments, replies, likes, @mentions, homepage shares, favourites, update requests, nicknames and avatars.

## Article 2 license Grant

2.1 Subject to your compliance with this Agreement, the Developer grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, revocable personal license to install and use the Software on devices you own. The license starts when you install the Software and ends when this Agreement terminates.

2.2 The license does not include access to, modification of, or distribution of the source code, except as granted by an applicable open-source license. The Software's non-public implementation (including Scheme adaptation, encrypted caches, plugin installation and elevation, and server communication protocols) remains protected by this Agreement.

2.3 The Software includes or links third-party open-source components (such as OpenVPN, FreeRDP and WebView2) and allows installation of third-party plugins. Those components and plugins are also governed by their own licenses and terms of service. If this Agreement conflicts with such licenses, it shall be interpreted so as not to deprive you of the rights they grant.

2.4 Apart from the rights expressly granted in this Agreement, the Developer reserves all rights in the Software and its derivative works. Third-party plugins, store resources and the trademarks and content they contain belong to their respective providers, and this Agreement does not change that ownership.

## Article 3 Restrictions

3.1 You may not rent, lend, sell or resell the Software, or use it for commercial operation or to provide hosting services to others, without the Developer's written permission.

3.2 You may not decompile, disassemble, reverse engineer, crack or circumvent license checks, or remove, alter or obscure copyright, trademark or license notices, except for compatibility interoperability expressly permitted by law.

3.3 You may not use the Software for activities that violate the laws of the People's Republic of China or of your jurisdiction, including unauthorized access to others' systems or data, network attacks, distribution of malicious programs, infringement of others' intellectual property or privacy, spam, or circumvention of access controls.

3.4 Auto-login and Token features may only be used for accounts and services you are entitled to access. You may not harvest others' credentials, access accounts without authorization or otherwise abuse accounts, and you may not replay, tamper with or mass-capture exported QR codes, or circumvent their session-key mechanism to obtain others' Tokens.

3.5 Cloud Sync is only for backing up and restoring your own data. You may not upload unlawful or harmful content, data you have no right to dispose of, or packages exported by others, or use the feature to circumvent storage limits or attack the Server.

3.6 You may not circumvent or undermine plugin installation checks, elevation flows, path safety checks, single-instance mutual exclusion or system service registration, or damage the integrity of the Software or affect other users by tampering with the application directory, registry or installed components.

3.7 Community Content must be truthful, lawful and not infringe others' rights. You may not post unlawful content, pornography or violence, defamation or insults, harassment, spam or fraudulent information. The Developer may remove or block violating content or restrict the community features of the accounts concerned.

## Article 4 User Data and Privacy

4.1 **Local data and account isolation.** The Software stores data per signed-in account under %APPDATA%\Kirara (users\<account id>), including the local database (LiteDB), encryption keys, credentials, caches and logs. A global layer (global) holds account-independent configuration, backgrounds and sign-in history; web data is stored under %LOCALAPPDATA%\Kirara\users\<account id>\webview2. Uninstalling the Software keeps this data by default; you may delete it manually.

4.2 **Encryption.** Account names, passwords, API keys, server addresses and RefreshTokens in Tokens are encrypted with AES-256-GCM, with keys protected by Windows DPAPI (current-user scope). Cached backgrounds, avatars, covers, Scheme icons and .ovpn configurations are also stored encrypted. Keep your Windows account and sign-in credentials safe; the Developer is not liable for disclosure caused by others accessing your session or unencrypted copies.

4.3 **Server communication.** To provide account authentication, template and Scheme configuration sync, comments, notification push, feeds, resource downloads, Cloud Sync and OpenVPN configuration distribution, the Software transmits account identifiers, session tokens, a device identifier, local version numbers and content you submit. Beyond these necessary cases, the Software does not upload local data without your action.

4.4 **Device identifier and sign-in.** The Software binds sign-in tokens to a device identifier protected by DPAPI. When you sign out, the Server revokes only the current device's token and does not affect the same account signed in on other devices.

4.5 **Cloud Sync data.** Uploads are data packages encrypted per account. The Server stores them isolated per user, does not parse their contents, and keeps only the latest package of each type per user. You may delete cloud data in the Software at any time. The Developer is not liable for access or loss caused by compromised account credentials or cloud storage failure.

4.6 **Visibility of Community Content.** Comments, replies, likes, shares, update requests, nicknames and avatars you submit are stored on the Server and may be shown to other users or administrators and used for interaction notifications. Content posted with "Private mention" is visible only to you and the mentioned users; that audience is fixed when the content is posted. Do not submit personal information you do not want others to know in Community Content.

4.7 **Clipboard and file transfer.** Remote desktop Schemes may synchronize clipboard text and files between the local device and the remote session; web drag-and-drop passes files you select to the corresponding page. These transfers are triggered by your actions; confirm that the target environment is trustworthy before copying or dropping sensitive content.

4.8 **Logs.** The Software generates local runtime, crash, auto-login and remote desktop diagnostic logs to troubleshoot problems. They do not record plaintext passwords or Token ciphertext. Review log contents before sending them to the Developer.

4.9 **Export, import and deletion.** You may export an encrypted data package (instances, Tokens, preferences and Notification Center content; the license consent flag and feed cards are excluded). Exported packages contain sensitive credentials; keep them safe. "Clear cache", "Clear local data" and uninstalling remove the corresponding data, and those operations cannot be undone. "Clear local data" also removes accounts remembered on the sign-in page and the start-with-Windows entries registered by this version.

## Article 5 Network Services and Third Parties

5.1 Online features depend on Internet connectivity and Server availability. Network interruptions, carrier failures, maintenance or force majeure may make features unavailable or delayed; the Developer does not warrant uninterrupted or perpetual online services and is not liable for losses arising from this.

5.2 Third-party services targeted by Schemes are provided and maintained independently by their operators. The Developer is not responsible for their content, availability, security or data processing. You must comply with their terms of service and privacy policies.

5.3 When using remote connections such as OpenVPN, ensure that your conduct complies with the rules of the target network and applicable law; some regions restrict virtual private networks. Connection quality depends on the network environment, server configuration and carrier policies, and the Developer does not warrant stable or successful connections or any particular speed.

5.4 Resources, plugins and extensions in the App Store are uploaded and maintained by the Developer or third-party providers. Plugins may run as separate processes, require administrator rights or modify local files and system components; their functionality, security, compatibility and legality are the provider's responsibility. Confirm that the source is trustworthy before installing. System faults, data loss, security incidents or disputes caused by installing or using third-party plugins are for you and the provider to resolve. The Developer may delist, block or remove store content.

5.5 Homepage feed cards (image, video, HTML) are delivered by the Server and their content is the publisher's responsibility. Do not interact with elements in a card unless you are satisfied that it is safe.

5.6 Accounts with administrator rights may access the web management console through the Software to manage users, Schemes, notifications, templates, feeds and download resources. Administrative actions affect all users; follow the management rules. The operator bears the consequences of exceeding authority, abuse or operational error.

## Article 6 System Permissions and Security

6.1 Installing, upgrading and uninstalling may require administrator rights to write to the installation directory, register the system service (KiraraVpnHelper, which starts OpenVPN as LocalSystem), install or load the virtual network adapter driver (TAP/Wintun) and install optional components. The installer may migrate or clean up directories and registry entries of previous versions.

6.2 The Software can stay resident in the system tray and, according to your settings, writes a start-with-Windows registry entry (HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Run) and an "at logon" scheduled task (registered by the Software through KiraraVpnHelper). Plugin installation and removal in the App Store may go through an elevation flow. These permissions are used only as required for the features.

6.3 Obtain the Software and updates only from the Developer's official channels. Installers, cracked builds or modified builds from unknown sources may contain malicious code, and the Developer accepts no responsibility for them.

6.4 You are responsible for the security of your account credentials (username, password, API keys, Tokens and RefreshTokens) and of the access rights to services you manage, including using strong passwords, not disclosing credentials and signing out promptly on shared devices. You bear losses caused by inadequate safekeeping.

6.5 If you find a security vulnerability, report it through the Developer's published channels; do not publicly disclose it or exploit it against others before it is fixed.

6.6 QR codes exported from Token manager contain encrypted Tokens, and anyone who obtains such a code may import it through the official client. Display it in private, avoid screenshots, forwarding or prolonged public display; scan sessions expire.

## Article 7 Software Updates

7.1 The Software checks for and downloads updates and starts the installer after you confirm. Updates may fail due to the system environment, permissions, third-party security software or files in use; back up your data before important operations.

7.2 Release notes are shown version by version. A release marked as important must be installed before you can continue using the Software; declining it may make some online features unavailable.

7.3 Updates may change the interface, features or data storage. The Developer is not liable for configuration changes or compatibility issues after an update but will make reasonable efforts to keep data usable.

## Article 8 Disclaimer

8.1 The Software is provided "AS IS", without any express or implied warranty, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, non-infringement and data integrity. The Developer does not warrant that the Software is free of defects, uninterrupted or compatible with all hardware and software environments.

8.2 Although the Software encrypts and verifies cached resources, the Developer is not liable for local data corruption, loss or disclosure caused by system faults, disk failure, malware or third-party attacks. Back up important data regularly.

8.3 Third-party programs bundled with or linked by the Software are provided in their own state, and the Developer gives no warranty as to their defects, security or compatibility. The Developer is not liable for data loss, service interruption, connection failure, business loss or third-party service failure arising from use of the Software.

8.4 The Developer does not warrant the truthfulness, legality or accuracy of Community Content and is not liable for interactions, disputes or losses between users. The Developer also gives no guarantee as to the integrity, security or availability of files obtained through the Download Manager, web downloads, app updates or Cloud Sync, or the durability of cloud storage.

## Article 9 Limitation of Liability

9.1 To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Developer and its affiliates are not liable for indirect, incidental, special, punitive or consequential damages (including lost profits, data loss, business interruption or loss of goodwill) arising from the use of or inability to use the Software, whether based on contract, tort (including negligence) or any other legal theory.

9.2 The Software is provided free of charge. The aggregate liability of the Developer and its affiliates is limited to the amount you actually paid for the Software; if you paid nothing, the limit is RMB 100.

9.3 The Developer is not liable for service interruption or data loss caused by force majeure (natural disasters, war, government action, power or network failure, large-scale malicious attacks, etc.). This Article does not apply to personal injury caused by the Developer's wilful misconduct or gross negligence, or to liability that law does not allow to be limited.

## Article 10 Intellectual Property

10.1 The copyright, trademark and other intellectual property rights in the Software (including program code, interface design, icons, documentation, name and marks) belong to the Developer and its licensors and are protected by the laws of the People's Republic of China and international intellectual property law. Except for the license expressly granted, you may not use, copy or disseminate them.

10.2 Content you create, upload or manage through the Software (instance configurations, comments, files, etc.) belongs to you or the respective rights holders. You grant the Developer a non-exclusive, royalty-free license, transferable as part of operating the service, solely to provide the service to you (storage, sync, display, push, backup and presenting Community Content you submit to other users).

10.3 The Developer may use feedback, suggestions or improvements you provide to improve the product without further consent or payment; you represent that such feedback does not infringe third-party rights.

## Article 11 Term, Termination and Changes

11.1 This Agreement takes effect when you install or use the Software and continues until terminated. You may terminate it at any time by uninstalling the Software; uninstalling removes program files and registered system services but keeps local data under %APPDATA%\Kirara by default.

11.2 If you breach this Agreement, the Developer may terminate the license and require you to stop using the Software, uninstall it and delete all copies.

11.3 Provisions that by their nature should survive termination (including disclaimers, limitation of liability, intellectual property, governing law and dispute resolution) remain in effect; Community Content you have uploaded and Cloud Sync data are handled under Article 11.4.

11.4 You may delete Community Content and cloud data in the Software; to close your account or delete account-related data, contact the Developer through official channels.

11.5 The Developer may update this Agreement to reflect feature or legal changes. The updated Agreement is published in the Software with a version and effective date; material changes will be notified in the Software and may require you to read and accept the updated Agreement before continuing.

11.6 After an updated Agreement takes effect, your continued use of the Software constitutes acceptance; if you do not agree, stop using and uninstall the Software.

11.7 Your consent is recorded locally per signed-in account. The Settings Center provides a "Withdraw license agreement" entry; withdrawing closes the Software immediately, and you must accept the Agreement again before creating an Instance.

## Article 12 Governing Law and Dispute Resolution

12.1 The formation, validity, interpretation, performance and dispute resolution of this Agreement are governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China (excluding conflict-of-law rules). Where this Agreement refers to third-party licenses, their own governing terms apply to those parts.

12.2 Disputes arising from this Agreement shall first be resolved through friendly negotiation; failing that, either party may bring an action before the competent people's court at the Developer's domicile. During litigation, the remaining provisions continue to be performed except for the matters in dispute.

## Article 13 Miscellaneous

13.1 **Severability.** If any provision is held invalid or unenforceable, it shall be modified or severed to the minimum extent permitted by law, and the remaining provisions remain in effect.

13.2 **Entire agreement and waiver.** This Agreement, together with other policies published in the Software, constitutes the entire agreement and supersedes prior oral or written agreements. The Developer's failure or delay in exercising a right is not a waiver of that right.

13.3 **Contact.** If you have questions about this Agreement or the Software, contact the Developer through the official channels it publishes.

> If you have read and agree to the above terms, please click the Agree button below.

